From 2b195f60e3c029bf7ae8ef366355f9f8c9318c71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 03:55:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02247/11362] [outer-loop] ARC loop iter 1: frontier-distance
 navigation -> 3 levels from scratch (+m0r0)

Loop: baseline 2 levels (lp85,sp80). Tried BFS-search-order -> REGRESSED to 0 (killed the
deep-ride lp85/sp80 need) -> rejected per gate. Kept the orthogonal win: frontier-distance
navigation (StepwiseExplorer walks to the shallowest frontier via known forward edges when
reachable, else RESET+replay) ON TOP of the DFS-forward search order. Cheaper backtracking
-> more state coverage per budget -> m0r0 now solves from scratch (was no-advance). Net
2->3 levels, no regression (lp85/sp80 kept). r11l still open (a search-completeness problem,
not nav-cost). Replay path unaffected (11/11).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
